\f0\b0 \
Next to Karadere. \
\
Topog: many deep valleys, broken up. So, the area is marginal for farming.. few volcanic outcrops.\
\

\f1\b A\uc0\u287 \u305 l:
\f0\b0  There is one mudbrick building left, with stone foundation at the entrance. \
\
Flat roof, upheld by a central pole. Probably used for lambs. Has a door, very warm inside. Another one, the whole width of the fold is roofed, open in front, as usual. There is a division between entrance and roofed fold. Shepherd's hut is at the entrance which adjoins the corner of the stone wall. Huge beams holding up the roof of the fold, which has fallen in. \
